## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: pis, Language: Pijin, Number of verses: 21
## References: Gordon, Raymond G. Jr, ed. (2005). "Pijin, a Language of Solomon Islands". Ethnologue. Retrieved 12 October 2008. ; Lee, Ernest W. (1996). "Solomon Islands Pijin in Education". In Mugler, France; Lynch, John (eds.). Pacific Languages in Education. Suva, Fiji: Bluebird Printery. pp. 191–205. ; Pijin Dictionary: https://www.webonary.org/pijin/

